menu "pocket-tank"
    choice POCKET_TANK_WORLD
        prompt "The WORLD this bin is: the terrarium (lizards) or the aquarium (pocket-tank's fish)"
        default POCKET_TANK_WORLD_TERRARIUM
        help
            One core, a bin per world (common/world.h PT_WORLD, PLAN.md D11), compiled in - never
            chosen at run time. It picks the brain (the model and the tokenizer world.h names), the
            packs a tank holds, the goal set, the locomotion (the walk, or the swim) and the toolbox.
            The terrarium is the default; the aquarium is today's pocket-tank fish tank. Build the
            aquarium with SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.aquarium" (with a board's
            overlay after it: "sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.round;sdkconfig.aquarium") into its own
            build directory and sdkconfig.
        config POCKET_TANK_WORLD_TERRARIUM
            bool "terrarium: the lizards, walking (PT_WORLD 2)"
        config POCKET_TANK_WORLD_AQUARIUM
            bool "aquarium: pocket-tank's fish, swimming (PT_WORLD 1)"
    endchoice
    config POCKET_TANK_DISPLAY_SH8601
        bool "Drive the Waveshare 1.8in AMOLED (SH8601 / CO5300 over QSPI)"
        default n
        help
            Enable for the real board. Off = stub display port (QEMU / compile-only).
    config POCKET_TANK_ROUND
        bool "The ROUND build: a 466 px bowl for the Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-1.75C"
        default n
        help
            The tank's world is compiled in: off = the 448x368 rectangle (the
            1.8 board; on a 1.75C that image still runs, the frame shown inside
            the circle). On = TANK_ROUND, the bowl that fills the round glass;
            that image shows nothing on a 1.8. Build it with
            SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.round" into its
            own build directory and sdkconfig (docs/board-amoled-1.75c.md).
    config POCKET_TANK_WATCH
        bool "The WATCH build: a 410x502 PORTRAIT tank for the Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-2.06"
        default n
        depends on !POCKET_TANK_ROUND
        help
            On = TANK_WATCH: a tall tank the way a watch is worn, with the
            round corners of its glass; that image shows nothing on the
            other boards. Off, the 448x368 rectangle image still runs on a
            watch, on its side and centred in the glass. Build it with
            SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.watch" into its
            own build directory and sdkconfig (docs/board-amoled-2.06-watch.md).
    config POCKET_TANK_SQUARE
        bool "The SQUARE build: a 480x480 tank for the Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-2.16"
        default n
        depends on !POCKET_TANK_ROUND && !POCKET_TANK_WATCH
        help
            On = TANK_SQUARE: the tank fills the 2.16's square glass; that
            image shows nothing on the other boards. Build it with
            SDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.square" into its
            own build directory and sdkconfig (docs/board-amoled-2.16.md).
    config POCKET_TANK_TOUCH_FT3168
        bool "Read the FT3168 capacitive touch (taps / holds)"
        default n
    config POCKET_TANK_AUDIO_ES8311
        bool "Play the sound bank through the ES8311 codec + NS4150B amp (I2S)"
        default n
        help
            Enable for the real board (docs/AUDIO.md). Off = stub audio port: cues compile, nothing plays.
    config POCKET_TANK_NO_PIE
        bool "Disable the PIE SIMD inference kernel (scalar dot products)"
        default n
        help
            Enable for a QEMU build if the emulator lacks ESP32-S3 PIE support.
    config POCKET_TANK_CARD
        bool "microSD card library for the 1.8 (compile-only, UNVERIFIED on hardware)"
        default n
        depends on POCKET_TANK_DISPLAY_SH8601 && !POCKET_TANK_ROUND && !POCKET_TANK_WATCH && !POCKET_TANK_SQUARE
        help
            The card library (issue #4, phase 4): the 1.8's microSD slot as a
            library of packs. The PACKS page under ADVANCED lists the PTPK
            files in /packs on the card, checks them before use, installs
            them into the board's own flash (the `storage` partition, 0x6000
            to 0x10000) so a tank never depends on the card being in its
            slot, and removes them. The card is only ever read: never
            written, never formatted. On = PT_CARD 1 (common/world.h): the
            card port (main/card_port_sh8601.c), the pack store, the library
            and the PACKS page are compiled in, with the spare pack slots
            they need.

            NO SHIPPED IMAGE ENABLES THIS. It has never run on a board: the
            port is written from the vendor's schematic and BSP and
            compiled, nothing more. docs/card-library.md says what is
            sourced and what is not; docs/board-amoled-1.8-card.md is the
            bench test that would settle it. The 1.8 only: its slot is on
            GPIO 1, 2 and 3 and the expander's EXIO7, pins the other boards
            use for something else, so the option is not offered for them
            and the port refuses to start unless the 1.8 answered on I2C.

            It needs FAT long file names (sdkconfig.defaults sets
            CONFIG_FATFS_LFN_HEAP: a .ptpk name has a four-letter
            extension) and a FAT12/16/32 card - an exFAT card, the usual
            factory format from 64 GB, is not readable: format it FAT32.
    config POCKET_TANK_CARD_SPI
        bool "Card library: reach the card in SPI mode (sdspi on SPI3_HOST) instead of SDMMC 1-bit"
        default n
        depends on POCKET_TANK_CARD
        help
            An ALTERNATIVE to try if the card does not mount the vendor's
            way (SDMMC, 1 bit: the default). The card is reached over SPI
            on SPI3_HOST (the display has SPI2) and its chip select, the
            expander's EXIO7, is held LOW for the whole visit
            (board_sd_select(true); the sdspi driver is given no
            chip-select pin). Equally UNVERIFIED on hardware.

            A card that has seen EXIO7 low at CMD0 stays in SPI mode until
            its power is cycled and will not answer SDMMC after: once this
            has been tried, take the card out and put it back before going
            back to SDMMC.
    config POCKET_TANK_CARD_PIN_CLK
        int "Card CLK (SCK in SPI mode) GPIO"
        default 2
        range 0 48
        depends on POCKET_TANK_CARD
        help
            The slot's clock: net SCK in the SD-CARD block of the vendor's
            schematic (ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-1.8.pdf) and BSP_SD_CLK
            (GPIO_NUM_2) in the vendor's BSP (bsp/esp32_s3_touch_amoled_1_8).
            UNVERIFIED on this repo's hardware. Not a pin the board uses:
            0 (BOOT), 4-9, 11, 12, 14-16, 21, 45, 46 are the display, I2C,
            touch, audio and the amp's (main/board_pins.h; the build
            refuses the display, I2C and touch ones).
    config POCKET_TANK_CARD_PIN_CMD
        int "Card CMD (MOSI in SPI mode) GPIO"
        default 1
        range 0 48
        depends on POCKET_TANK_CARD
        help
            The slot's command line: net MOSI (= the card's CMD) in the
            SD-CARD block of the vendor's schematic and BSP_SD_CMD
            (GPIO_NUM_1) in the vendor's BSP. UNVERIFIED on this repo's
            hardware. Not a pin the board uses (see the CLK pin's help).
    config POCKET_TANK_CARD_PIN_D0
        int "Card D0 (MISO in SPI mode) GPIO"
        default 3
        range 0 48
        depends on POCKET_TANK_CARD
        help
            The slot's data line 0: net MISO (= the card's D0) in the
            SD-CARD block of the vendor's schematic and BSP_SD_D0
            (GPIO_NUM_3) in the vendor's BSP. UNVERIFIED on this repo's
            hardware. Not a pin the board uses (see the CLK pin's help).
            The card's chip select (SDCS = CD/DAT3) is not a GPIO: it is
            bit 7 of the TCA9554 expander's output register at I2C 0x20
            (EXIO7, main/board_pins.h) - fixed, not configurable here.
endmenu
